<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17034" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτερπ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unpleasing, joyless,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					19.354
				</span></i>
			; of the nether world, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυας καὶ ἀτερπέα χῶρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.94
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτρῃς . . καὶ ἀτερπέῑ
				χώρῳ,</span> of a rocky shore, <i><span class="en">
				7.279
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νούσων ἑσμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					685
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				37.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					293
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					4.114
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτερπέστερον ἐς ἀκρόασιν</span>
			<i>less attractive</i> to the ear, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦχοι ἀ.,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτερπεῖς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Po.</u>
				994.23
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.82
			</span></i> K.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ τις ὑπερβάλλοι τὸ μέτριον τὰ
					ἐπιτερπέστατα ἀτερπέστατα ἂν γίγνοιτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					233
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.396
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			); of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ κακὸς ὀρχηστής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cor.</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πῶς, οὐκ ἀ. ἱστορείσθω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					14.237
				</span></i>
			; but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ζῆν</span>”
				<i>without enjoyment,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1100d
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
